Add `axoupdater = { version = "0.10", features = ["blocking"] }` and wrap it the way `loadout/src/update.rs` does:

```rust
let mut updater = AxoUpdater::new_for("artefacto");
if updater.load_receipt().is_err() {
    return Ok(Outcome::NotManaged);
}
if check_only {
    return Ok(if updater.is_update_needed_sync()? {
        Outcome::UpdateAvailable
    } else {
        Outcome::AlreadyCurrent
    });
}
match updater.run_sync()? { ... }
```

Four outcomes, exactly loadout's: `Updated { from, to }`, `AlreadyCurrent`, `UpdateAvailable`, `NotManaged`. `NotManaged` prints the installer command rather than erroring — that is the approved "no button for those people", and it is what somebody who ran `cargo install` needs to read.

Exit codes are a contract in this codebase (`src/client.rs:22`), so they are chosen deliberately and documented rather than falling out of `Result`.

The README's "there is no network" becomes untrue the moment this merges, so it changes here.

Record the built binary's size before and after. `q-weight` deserves a number, not an adjective.
